    "status": "answered",
    "answer": "The model catalog enables a framework for automatic model dispatch, but automatic dispatch is not yet fully implemented. The current router still uses `CHAT_FAST_*` and `CHAT_DEEP_*` settings; catalog eligibility is groundwork for automatic selection, not an automatic dispatch change. The model catalog defines metadata including task preferences, capabilities, and context/output limits, which are necessary for future automatic routing. However, the implementation plan indicates that automatic dispatch requires further steps such as discovering installed models, maintaining health observations, building bounded context, adding a task classifier, ranking models, and persisting selection reasons. These steps are planned but not yet completed.",
    "citations": [
        {
            "source_id": "model-catalog",
            "start_line": 1,
            "end_line": 30,
            "quote": "# Model catalog and task routing\n\n`data/model-catalog.json` is the versioned, validated inventory. Override its path\nwith `MODEL_CATALOG_PATH`. Invalid catalogs fail startup. `GET /models` returns the\ninventory, current fast/deep selections, and any configured models missing from it.\nThe current router still uses `CHAT_FAST_*` and `CHAT_DEEP_*`; catalog eligibility\nis groundwork for automatic selection, not an automatic dispatch change."
        },
        {
            "source_id": "model-catalog",
            "start_line": 36,
            "end_line": 52,
            "quote": "Next implementation steps:\n\n1. Discover installed Ollama models and deployment metadata from provider APIs;\n   record identity/revision, source and freshness for each observation. Merge\n   observations without overwriting operator preferences.\n2. Maintain time-limited health observations separately from the static catalog.\n   Distinguish installed, loaded, reachable, authorized, busy, and unavailable.\n3. Build bounded per-turn context and estimate token requirements before selection.\n4. Add a tested task classifier and enforce model **and adapter** capabilities.\n5. Rank eligible, healthy models using task evaluations, latency, queue pressure,\n   data-locality policy, and cost. Provide an explicit fallback when none qualify.\n6. Persist the selected model and selection reason on each task/turn. Show that\n   actual selection in the reply bubble; global fast/deep labels will be insufficient.\n\nStart with deterministic policies and a golden routing set. Introduce a learned\nrouter only after collecting evidence that it improves the decisions."
        }
    ],
    "missing_evidence": [
        "Evidence of current automatic dispatch implementation",
        "Details on when automatic dispatch will be enabled"
    ]
}
